 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of slices (`slices`) and occlusion samples (`uOcclusionSamplesCount`) per pixel.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the accumulator texture, instance/group ID textures, and the `sGroupMembership` buffer.
-*   **Strengths:** Integrates semantic segmentation (instance/group IDs) directly into the volume rendering pass, reducing the need for separate post-processing passes. The use of precomputed occlusion samples can accelerate depth-ordering effects.
-*   **Limitations:** Relies on precomputed occlusion samples, which may limit dynamic occlusion scenarios. The requirement for `std430` buffers and specific texture layouts may increase implementation complexity on some hardware.
-*   **When to use:** When semantic segmentation is required alongside volume visualization, or when occlusion-aware depth ordering is critical and can be approximated by precomputed samples.
-*   **When not to use:** For scenes with highly dynamic occlusion that cannot be precomputed, or when hardware does not support `std430` buffers efficiently.
